PORTIONS FROM TIMM
------------------
network.py carries the inference path of timm's VisionTransformer, Block,
Attention, LayerScale, PatchEmbed, Mlp and LayerNorm2d (timm 1.0.15,
https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models), Copyright Ross Wightman,
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 -- the same licence as mozo, whose LICENSE
at the repository root carries the full text. EoMT's own models/eomt.py states
that it adapts portions of timm the same way.

ON THE WEIGHTS
--------------
Each published checkpoint is MIT, stated on the authors' Hugging Face model card
(`license: mit`) and by the repository's LICENSE. The backbones were initialised
from Meta's DINOv2 with registers, released under Apache-2.0. EoMT checkpoints
built on DINOv3 (Meta's custom licence) or on Web-SSL DINO 7B (CC-BY-NC-4.0) are
not carried. Neither is the Cityscapes checkpoint: Cityscapes' licence forbids
commercial use of the dataset or any derivative work and names trained models as
derivative works.

THE TRAINING DATA
-----------------
The coco-panoptic-* variants were trained on COCO 2017 panoptic: annotations
CC-BY-4.0, images Flickr photographs under their owners' licences.
ade20k-semantic-large was trained on ADE20K: annotations BSD-3-Clause, while MIT
CSAIL's terms make the images available for non-commercial research and
educational use only. Neither set of terms is a licence on the weights, which the
authors release under MIT; they are stated so a user can judge their own use.
Each weights directory's NOTICE says the same for its variant.
